    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we find the prime factorization of both numbers.\n\nFor 40:\n\\[ 40 = 2 \\times 20 \\]\n\\[ 20 = 2 \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ 10 = 2 \\times 5 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 40 is:\n\\[ 40 = 2^3 \\times 5 \\]\n\nFor 48:\n\\[ 48 = 2 \\times 24 \\]\n\\[ 24 = 2 \\times 12 \\]\n\\[ 12 = 2 \\times 6 \\]\n\\[ 6 = 2 \\times 3 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 48 is:\n\\[ 48 = 2^4 \\times 3 \\]\n\nNext, we identify the common prime factors and the lowest power of each common prime factor. The common prime factor of 40 and 48 is 2. The lowest power of 2 in both factorizations is \\(2^3\\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor (GCF) of 40 and 48 is:\n\\[ 2^3 = 8 \\]\n\nSo, the answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{8} \\]",
